I'll explore the project context around columns, profiles, and project handling before proposing changes.Let me read the related board components to understand column definitions, modals, and how tasks are created.## Review & Understand the Task

- Allow a board column to **define a project**; tasks created in that column must get that `project_id`.
- Persist the choice with the column (sprint columns live on `board.columns`, kanban columns too).
- In the column header, show the **project icon next to the profile avatars**, but only when that project differs from the active project.
- No visual noise for same-project columns (icon is opt-in per column).

## Information Gathered

- `SprintBoardModals.vue` is the shared column dialog (`boardType` = `sprint` | `kanban`) and already emits `{ title, status, icon, color, profiles }`.
- `src/store/kanban.js`:
  - `sprintColumns`, `defaultSprintColumns`, `materializeSprintColumns`, `addSprintColumn`, `updateSprintColumn`, `newSprintTask` — **no** `project_id` today.
  - `buildViewColumns` / `addColumn` / `updateColumn` already support `project_id`.
- `SprintBoardView.vue` and `KanbanBoardView.vue` forward `column-created` / `column-updated` to the store (they must forward `project_id` too).
- `SprintTaskCard.vue` already renders the task project icon only when `project_id !== $project.project_id` — same rule to reuse for the column header.

## Changes Summary

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `src/store/kanban.js` | Sprint columns carry `project_id` (defaults, getter, materialize, add, update); `newSprintTask` falls back to the destination column's project. |
| `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardModals.vue` | Column dialog gets a project picker; new tasks default to the destination column's project. |
| `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardView.vue` | Forward `project_id` on column create/update. |
| `src/components/kanban/board/KanbanBoardView.vue` | Forward `project_id` on column create/update. |
| `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardColumn.vue` | Show the column project icon next to the profile avatars (only when different from the active project). |

## The Changes

